{"id": "EUVD-2026-102279", "enisaUuid": "0c212f90-2886-3d34-a08b-023574b37e1e", "description": "Game Music Emu (libgme) through 0.6.5 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the AY loader get_data function caused by an integer underflow in the track-table bounds check. Attackers can supply a crafted ZXAYEMUL file with an oversized track table to read past the file buffer via gme_track_info or gme_start_track, crashing libgme consumers.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:10:16", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libgme-ay-track-table-underflow-oob-read", "https://github.com/libgme/game-music-emu/blob/9e23d10f9fd2a6a2f33b10912dd8dc7153258995/gme/Ay_Emu.cpp#L53-L80", "https://github.com/libgme/game-music-emu/commit/ae10a8f05479e3c8f80429e7a59759fed06f8c13", "https://github.com/libgme/game-music-emu", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/game-music-emu-libgme-through-0.6.5-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-ay-loader"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wm76-g833-ghjv", "CVE-2026-111152"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "56786aa1-c317-336c-87f5-7296736a1e6a", "product": {"name": "game-music-emu", "vendor": {"name": "libgme"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.6.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a649c100-0069-3721-b4a9-370d5cc5e2e8", "vendor": {"name": "libgme"}}], "isExploited": false}